# check_claims.py hashes the forcing CSV and compares it with the SHA-256 in
# README.md. Git's default autocrlf on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout,
# which changes those bytes and fails the check on Windows clones only.
#
# The model output depends on it too: a CRLF file still parses, but the hash in
# the README would no longer describe the file that produced the benchmark.
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.pyx   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
